   "text": "Built and checked. The camera is left showing the section.\n\n**What's there (cols 10\u201360, all 1x):**\n- Spider portal at col 10, cube portal at col 60 (on the floor band, rows 0\u20132)\n- Roof of blocks in rows 6\u20137 right across the section \u2014 underside at y=180, i.e. six blocks up, so the spider's ceiling surface is exactly 6 blocks above the floor surface\n- Hazards:\n  - floor spikes: cols 13\u201317 (a four-wide run guarding the entry), then pairs at 25\u201326, 37\u201338, 49\u201350\n  - ceiling spikes hanging from the roof: pairs at 20\u201321, 32\u201333, 44\u201345, and 58\u201359 to force the drop into the cube portal\n\nSo the run is flip up, flip down, flip up\u2026 eight flips in total, and it ends as a cube on the ground.\n\n**Playability check** (`verify_section`, cols 300\u20131830, from the level start): **possible**, with 8 presses, every timing window **104\u2013117 ms** \u2014 no frame-perfect inputs. Judged against normal/medium it's `in_band: true`, no violations. The exit state is mode `cube`, gravity normal, standing on the floor at x=1830, so the cube portal does trigger.\n\nOne thing worth knowing: a cube jump carried into the portal could float over a two-wide first spike pair to skip the opening flip, and that shortcut was frame-perfect (20.8 ms). That's why the first floor hazard is four blocks wide \u2014 it closes that line and leaves only the wide-window route.\n\nI haven't playtested it in the game (that needs to be its own turn, since this one changed the level). Want me to playtest it?",
